      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Machines need makers. The m-/wa-",
          "class manufactures them from verbs:",
          "",
          "   kusanifu  ->  msanifu   designer",
          "   kusikiliza -> msikilizaji listener",
          "   kuandika  ->  mwandishi  writer",
          "",
          "Two tails: -aji for the habitual",
          "doer, -i/-shi for the office or",
          "craft. Both take wa- in the plural:",
          "",
          "   wasanifu, wasikilizaji, waandishi",
          "",
          "Hear them:                         Press 1"
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Msanifu. Msikilizaji. Mwandishi. Waandishi."
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "The borrowed professionals behave",
          "differently on the card face:",
          "",
          "   kocha  ->  makocha   coaches",
          "   dereva ->  madereva  drivers",
          "   rais   ->  marais    presidents",
          "",
          "ma- plurals — but PEOPLE agreement:",
          "",
          "   Makocha wale wanafundisha vizuri.",
          "   Those coaches teach well.",
          "",
          "Hear them:                         Press 1",
          "",
